  "evidencia": "Page: Princess Mafalda of Savoy. Sentence: Princess Mafalda of Savoy (2 November 1902 – 27 August 1944) was the second daughter of King Victor Emmanuel III of Italy and his wife Elena of Montenegro.\nPage: Princess Mafalda of Savoy. Sentence: The future King Umberto II of Italy was her younger brother.\nPage: Umberto II of Italy. Sentence: Umberto II (Italian: \"Umberto Nicola Tommaso Giovanni Maria di Savoia\" ; 15 September 190418 March 1983), was the last King of Italy.\nPage: Umberto II of Italy. Sentence: He reigned for 34 days, from 9 May 1946 to 12 June 1946, although he had been \"de facto\" head of state since 1944, and was nicknamed the May King (Italian: Re di Maggio ).\nPage: SS Principessa Mafalda. Sentence: Named after Princess Mafalda of Savoy, second daughter of King Victor Emmanuel III, the ship entered NGI's South American service between Genoa and Buenos Aires in 1909.",
